        "problem": "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $10{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=40.$",
        "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =40 \\\\ 10{x}^{2}-(0)^{2} & =40 \\\\ 10{x}^{2}-0 & =40 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $(\\pm 2,0).$",
